workedExamples.solution_text:
Dilate horizontally by a factor of $3$ and vertically by a factor of $2$. Each base point $(u,v)$ becomes $(3u,2v)$.
The endpoints become $(-3,-\pi)$ and $(3,\pi)$. Both intercepts are $(0,0)$.
For the domain,
$\begin{aligned}-1&\le\frac{x}{3}\le1\\-3&\le x\le3\end{aligned}$
The range is $-\pi\le y\le\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-3.8,0)--(3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-3.9)--(0,3.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[curveblue,thick,domain=-pi/2:pi/2,samples=100,variable=\t] plot ({3*sin(deg(\t))},{2*\t});
\fill[curveblue] (-3,-pi) circle (1.8pt);
\fill[curveblue] (3,pi) circle (1.8pt);
\fill[curveblue] (0,0) circle (1.8pt);
\path (-3,-pi) node[above left] {$(-3,-\pi)$};
\path (3,pi) node[below right] {$(3,\pi)$};
\path (0,0) node[below right] {$(0,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Translate $2$ units right, reflect in the $x$-axis, then translate $\frac{\pi}{2}$ units up.
Each base point $(u,v)$ becomes $\left(u+2,\frac{\pi}{2}-v\right)$.
The three key points become $\left(1,-\frac{\pi}{2}\right)$, $(2,0)$ and $\left(3,\frac{\pi}{2}\right)$.
For the domain,
$\begin{aligned}-1&\le x-2\le1\\1&\le x\le3\end{aligned}$
The range is $-\frac{\pi}{2}\le y\le\frac{\pi}{2}$.
The $x$-intercept is $(2,0)$. There is no $y$-intercept because $0$ is outside the domain.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=13mm,y=12mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-0.4,0)--(3.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[curveblue,thick,domain=0:pi,samples=100,variable=\t] plot ({2+cos(deg(\t))},{pi/2-\t});
\fill[curveblue] (1,-pi/2) circle (1.8pt);
\fill[curveblue] (2,0) circle (1.8pt);
\fill[curveblue] (3,pi/2) circle (1.8pt);
\path (1,-pi/2) node[below right] {$\left(1,-\frac{\pi}{2}\right)$};
\path (2,0) node[below right] {$(2,0)$};
\path (3,pi/2) node[above left] {$\left(3,\frac{\pi}{2}\right)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Dilate horizontally by a factor of $\frac13$, then translate $\frac{\pi}{4}$ units down.
The domain remains $\mathbb R$. The range is $-\frac{3\pi}{4}<y<\frac{\pi}{4}$, with horizontal asymptotes $y=-\frac{3\pi}{4}$ and $y=\frac{\pi}{4}$.
At $x=0$,
$\begin{aligned}y&=\arctan 0-\frac{\pi}{4}\\y&=-\frac{\pi}{4}\end{aligned}$
For the $x$-intercept,
$\begin{aligned}0&=\arctan(3x)-\frac{\pi}{4}\\\arctan(3x)&=\frac{\pi}{4}\\3x&=1\\x&=\frac13\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=14mm,y=13mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-2.4,0)--(2.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-2.9)--(0,1.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,dashed] (-2.2,pi/4)--(2.2,pi/4);
\draw[black,dashed] (-2.2,-3*pi/4)--(2.2,-3*pi/4);
\path (-1.3,pi/4) node[above] {$y=\frac{\pi}{4}$};
\path (-1.3,-3*pi/4) node[below] {$y=-\frac{3\pi}{4}$};
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-2.2:2.2,samples=120] plot (\x,{rad(atan(3*\x))-pi/4});
\fill[curveblue] (0,-pi/4) circle (1.8pt);
\fill[curveblue] (1/3,0) circle (1.8pt);
\path (0,-pi/4) node[left] {$\left(0,-\frac{\pi}{4}\right)$};
\path (1/3,0) node[below right] {$\left(\frac13,0\right)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

