development.solution_text:
Apply a horizontal dilation by a factor of $2$ and a vertical dilation by a factor of $3$.
Each point $(x,y)$ becomes $(2x,3y)$.
The endpoints become $\left(-2,-\frac{3\pi}{2}\right)$ and $\left(2,\frac{3\pi}{2}\right)$. The origin stays fixed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.2cm,y=0.6cm]
\draw[->] (-2.7,0)--(2.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-5.5)--(0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=-1.5708:1.5708,samples=100,variable=\t] plot ({2*sin(deg(\t))},{3*\t});
\fill (-2,-4.7124) circle (2pt);
\fill (2,4.7124) circle (2pt);
\draw (-2,0.12)--(-2,-0.12) node[below] {$-2$};
\draw (2,0.12)--(2,-0.12) node[below] {$2$};
\node[left] at (0,4.7124) {$\frac{3\pi}{2}$};
\node[left] at (0,-4.7124) {$-\frac{3\pi}{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Translate the graph $1$ unit to the left, replacing $x$ with $x+1$.
The new equation is $y=\arccos(x+1)$.
The endpoints $(-1,\pi)$ and $(1,0)$ become $(-2,\pi)$ and $(0,0)$. The point $\left(0,\frac{\pi}{2}\right)$ becomes $\left(-1,\frac{\pi}{2}\right)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.4cm,y=1cm]
\draw[->] (-2.6,0)--(0.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.6)--(0,3.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=0:3.1416,samples=100,variable=\t] plot ({cos(deg(\t))-1},{\t});
\fill (-2,3.1416) circle (2pt);
\fill (0,0) circle (2pt);
\draw (-2,0.07)--(-2,-0.07) node[below] {$-2$};
\draw (-1,0.07)--(-1,-0.07) node[below] {$-1$};
\node[right] at (0,3.1416) {$\pi$};
\node[right] at (0,1.5708) {$\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Dilate vertically by a factor of $2$, then translate $\pi$ units down.
Double each asymptote value, then subtract $\pi$.
$y=2\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\right)-\pi=0$
$y=2\left(-\frac{\pi}{2}\right)-\pi=-2\pi$
At $x=0$, $y=2\arctan 0-\pi=-\pi$.
The $y$-intercept is $(0,-\pi)$. The curve approaches $y=0$ from below, so it has no $x$-intercept.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.7cm,y=0.7cm]
\draw[->] (-4.6,0)--(4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-7)--(0,0.7) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed] (-4.4,-6.2832)--(4.4,-6.2832);
\node[below] at (-3,-6.2832) {$y=-2\pi$};
\node[above] at (-3,0) {$y=0$};
\draw[thick,<->,domain=-4.4:4.4,samples=100] plot (\x,{2*rad(atan(\x))-3.1416});
\fill (0,-3.1416) circle (2pt);
\node[left] at (0,-3.1416) {$-\pi$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

