The horizontal dilation does not change the range, and the translation adds $\frac{\pi}{4}$ to each asymptote.
$y=\frac{\pi}{2}+\frac{\pi}{4}=\frac{3\pi}{4}$
$y=-\frac{\pi}{2}+\frac{\pi}{4}=-\frac{\pi}{4}$
For the $y$-intercept, substitute $x=0$.
$y=\arctan 0+\frac{\pi}{4}=\frac{\pi}{4}$
For the $x$-intercept, set $y=0$.
$\arctan(2x)=-\frac{\pi}{4}$
$2x=-1$
$x=-\frac{1}{2}$
